# class: ci-cd-integration
# schema: section | title | kind | summary | source
# source: docs/ci-cd-integration.md
# recipe: novel

intro | Why this works for every CI/CD tool | rationale | No CI-tool SDKs; sole integration point is POST /api/deployments; FR-06 codifies single-step adoption | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#why-this-works-for-every-cicd-tool
wire-endpoint | Endpoint URL | contract | POST {DEPLOYMENT_DASHBOARD_URL}/api/deployments | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#wire-contract-canonical
wire-auth | Authentication header | contract | X-Api-Key header; 401 on missing/invalid (FR-10) | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#wire-contract-canonical
wire-useragent | User-Agent header | recommendation | deployment-dashboard-notify/1.0 (+<tool>) for audit logs | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#wire-contract-canonical
wire-payload-required | Minimum payload (8 required fields) | contract | deployment_id, service, environment, version, status, run_url, run_number, actor | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#wire-contract-canonical
wire-payload-optional | Optional payload extensions | contract | parent_deployments + ref + sha (independently omittable per CR-0003 + CR-0004) | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#wire-contract-canonical
wire-length-caps | Field length caps (validation at ingest) | contract | deployment_id/service/environment/version/actor/ref: 200; run_url: 2048; sha: 64 (per CR-0008) | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#wire-contract-canonical
wire-status-codes | Failure responses | contract | 400 cross-service-parent/cycle; 401 missing-key; 409 duplicate (service,deployment_id); 422 missing-required/invalid-status/quoted-run_number | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#wire-contract-canonical
wire-idempotency | Idempotency model | contract | Append-only with deduplication key; CI/CD owns deployment_id; retry with same id -> 409; retry with new id -> new event | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#wire-contract-canonical
secrets | Required secrets | contract | DEPLOYMENT_DASHBOARD_URL (no trailing slash) + DEPLOYMENT_DASHBOARD_TOKEN | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#secrets
snippet-generic-shell | Generic shell snippet | snippet | curl -sf POST + Content-Type + X-Api-Key + User-Agent; $TOOL_PREFIX-prefixed deployment_id | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#generic-shell-snippet-works-in-any-cicd-tool
snippet-github-actions | GitHub Actions | snippet | Inline curl step; composite-action wrapper (.github/actions/notify/) preferred for input-validate + token-mask + cross-runner-OS | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#github-actions
snippet-azure-devops | Azure DevOps | snippet | PowerShell task with Invoke-RestMethod; secrets via variable group or pipeline-secret | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#azure-devops
snippet-jenkins | Jenkins | snippet | Declarative pipeline with post-success/post-failure notifyDashboard(); Credentials Binding plugin for secrets | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#jenkins
snippet-gitlab-ci | GitLab CI | snippet | .gitlab-ci.yml YAML anchor (notify-dashboard) + notify:success/notify:failure jobs in .post stage | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#gitlab-ci
snippet-other-tools | Other tools (CircleCI / Bitbucket / TeamCity / ...) | snippet | Use generic shell + map built-in variables | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#other-tools-circleci-bitbucket-pipelines-teamcity-
inprogress-pattern | In-progress + terminal pattern | how-to | Fire status=in-progress at deploy start; fire success/failure at deploy end; dashboard derives lastSuccessful + previousFailed | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#in-progress--terminal-pattern
troubleshooting | Troubleshooting guide | how-to | 401/422/404/timeout/silent-failure remedies | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#troubleshooting
attribution-header-overview | Event attribution - X-Progress-Reporter header (CR-0009) | contract | Optional request header on POST /api/deployments; cap 64 non-whitespace; persisted on event row to new progress_reporter column; surfaced on Read API responses (DeploymentEventResponse + CurrentDeployment + LastSuccessfulDeployment); ValidationProblemDetails 422 on violation reusing CR-0008 contract; namespace-by-convention only; applies to every push caller (inline curl, GHA composite, SDKs, webhook receivers, the fetcher) | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#event-attribution--x-progress-reporter-header
attribution-namespacing | Recommended namespacing convention | recommendation | <source-component>/<adapter-or-context> form - dashboard-fetcher/github-actions, ci-pipeline/gha-composite, ci-pipeline/<tool-slug>, manual/<operator-name>, webhook-receiver/<source>; convention not enforcement | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#recommended-namespacing--source-componentadapter-or-context
attribution-example | Inline curl example with X-Progress-Reporter | snippet | curl -sf POST with -H "X-Progress-Reporter: ci-pipeline/gha-composite" added to standard headers | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#example--inline-curl-with-attribution
pullmode-overview | Pull-mode alternative (optional, CR-0009 + ADR-0004) | rationale | Dashboard.Fetcher translates pull->push when push-mode unavailable; opt-in container; backend behaviour identical whether fetcher deployed; always sets X-Progress-Reporter dashboard-fetcher/<adapter-id>; MVP ships GHA adapter only | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#pull-mode-alternative-optional
pullmode-when-to-use | When to use pull-mode | how-to | No outbound network to dashboard (NFR-04); CI/CD offers no inline-script/composite hook; pipeline owned by team that won't accept notify-step change; centrally-operated backfill/catch-up of missed events | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#when-to-use-pull-mode
pullmode-env-vars | Required env vars (GitHub Actions adapter, MVP) | contract | DEPLOYMENT_DASHBOARD_URL + DEPLOYMENT_DASHBOARD_TOKEN + GHA_TOKEN (PAT, repo:deployments) + GHA_SOURCE_ID (owner/repo) + POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS (default 30) + INITIAL_FETCH_LIMIT (default 50 ceiling 500); env-var-only no .env files per project bindings | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#required-env-vars-github-actions-adapter-mvp
pullmode-rate-limit-cap | Self-imposed rate-limit cap (CR-0011) | contract | Two governance env-vars: FETCHER_RATE_LIMIT_ABSOLUTE (int requests / upstream window, unset by default) + FETCHER_RATE_LIMIT_PERCENTAGE (1..100, default 30). Precedence: absolute wins over percentage. Cap-reached behaviour: stop issuing CI/CD calls for window + resume at X-RateLimit-Reset without cursor advance + single INFO log per window. Leaky-bucket on upstream-observed Remaining (no fetcher-side counter); rationale anchored in ADR-0008. Scope: per upstream token / per adapter instance (not per source-id) since one PAT serves multiple repos. Reporting still per (adapter_id, source_id) via /api/fetcher/usage. | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#self-imposed-rate-limit-cap-cr-0011
pullmode-anonymous-mode | Anonymous-mode transport (zero-PAT installs) | contract | Fetcher boots without GHA_TOKEN (unauthenticated GitHub API; 60 req/h vs 5000 authed); read-only access only; supports -Demo flow in install.ps1 / start.ps1; placeholder token from compose; rate-limit cap still applies but at the much lower anonymous budget. Demo defaults: GHA_REPOSITORIES=[{owner:PostHog,repo:posthog}], FETCHER_POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS=60. | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#anonymous-mode-transport-zero-pat-installs
pullmode-cursor-model | Cursor model | contract | Restart-cursor lives on backend not fetcher; PUT after each successful poll cycle + GET on startup; opaque length-capped string <= 4KB; each adapter owns cursor shape per ADR-0004 Decision 2 | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#cursor-model
pullmode-first-fetch | First-fetch behaviour | contract | GET /api/fetcher/state returns 404 when no cursor exists; fetcher fetches at most INITIAL_FETCH_LIMIT events in first round then writes cursor; subsequent polls follow adapter natural pagination | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#first-fetch-behaviour
pullmode-failure-retry | Failure / retry posture | contract | Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience (AddStandardResilienceHandler, Polly v8 internally) for transient 5xx/timeouts; 409 from POST /api/deployments treated as success (ADR-0004 Decision 4); rate-limit signals (X-RateLimit-*) -> host pauses to reset; crash/restart = no event loss; 401 from backend loops at back-off; backend never affected by fetcher failure modes | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#failure--retry-posture
pullmode-resilience-invariant | Resilience-handler tuning invariant | contract | OptionsValidationException at build if CircuitBreaker.SamplingDuration < 2 x AttemptTimeout.Timeout; shipping config pins SamplingDuration=60s on both HttpClients (Write-API + GitHub-API); any future raise of AttemptTimeout above 30s MUST raise SamplingDuration to at least 2x new AttemptTimeout | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#resilience-handler-tuning-invariant
pullmode-local-dev | Local-dev opt-in | how-to | docker compose --profile fetcher up (or dev_env/start.ps1 -Fetcher / -Demo); defined in dev_env/docker-compose.local.yml under fetcher profile (inert by default); reuses literal API_TOKEN (local-dev-token-not-for-production) + targets gateway:80; GHA_TOKEN read from shell env (${GHA_TOKEN:-...}) | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#local-dev-opt-in
cross-references | Cross-references | links | SAD §1/2/4/7/8 + WBS MVP §1.4 + CI-CD Integration §1 | @docs/ci-cd-integration.md#cross-references